{"name":"Lily Pond Blue","hex":"#55707f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lily","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several flowers in the genus Lilium of the family Liliaceae, which includes a great many ornamental species.","Any of several species of herbaceous flower which may or may not resemble the genus Lilium in some way, and which are not closely related to it or each other."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["White ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lily"},{"term":"pond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inland body of standing water, either natural or man-made, that is smaller than a lake.","An inland body of standing water of any size that is fed by springs rather than by a river."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Chiefly in across the pond: the Atlantic Ocean."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pond"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lilium","blocks":[{"text":"Lilium is a genus of herbaceous flowering plants growing from bulbs, all with large and often prominent flowers. Lilies are a group of flowering plants which are important in culture and literature in much of the world. Most species are native to the Northern Hemisphere and their range is temperate climates and extends into the subtropics. Many other plants have \"lily\" in their common names, but do not belong to the same genus and are therefore not true lilies. True lilies are known to be highly toxic to cats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Lilium_candidum_1.jpg/330px-Lilium_candidum_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilium","wikidata":"Q5194627"},{"title":"Pond","blocks":[{"text":"A pond is a small, still, land-based body of water formed by pooling inside a depression, either naturally or artificially. A pond is smaller than a lake and there are no official criteria distinguishing the two, although defining a pond to be less than 5 hectares in area, less than 5 metres (16 ft) in depth and with less than 30% of its area covered by emergent vegetation helps in distinguishing the ecology of ponds from those of lakes and wetlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg/330px-Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pond","wikidata":"Q12719646"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/500px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/1280px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/500px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lilium longiflorum flower – 1. stigma, 2. style, 3. anthers, 4. filament, 5. tepal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALillium_Stamens.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Lily%2C_petal.jpg/500px-Lily%2C_petal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Lily%2C_petal.jpg/1280px-Lily%2C_petal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Lily%2C_petal.jpg/500px-Lily%2C_petal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lily, petal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALily%2C_petal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/2012-01-04_17-57-36-lys.jpg/500px-2012-01-04_17-57-36-lys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/2012-01-04_17-57-36-lys.jpg/1280px-2012-01-04_17-57-36-lys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/2012-01-04_17-57-36-lys.jpg/500px-2012-01-04_17-57-36-lys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stamen of lilium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2012-01-04_17-57-36-lys.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Lilium_candidum_M